 Pattern 2 — Sliding Window & Two Pointers
CORE IDEA: Process a "window" of elements by moving two pointers instead of re-scanning from scratch. Turns O(n²) into O(n).2
The Pattern
// Max sum of k consecutive elements — naive: O(n*k)
// Sliding window: O(n)

function maxWindowSum(array $arr, int $k): int {
    $windowSum = array_sum(array_slice($arr, 0, $k));
    $maxSum = $windowSum;
    for ($i = $k; $i < count($arr); $i++) {
        $windowSum += $arr[$i] - $arr[$i - $k]; // slide: add right, drop left
        $maxSum = max($maxSum, $windowSum);
    }
    return $maxSum;
}
Where This Pattern Applies in Your Work
Use case	Window = ?	Why it matters
