 Pattern 3 — Recursion & Tree Traversal
CORE IDEA: A recursive function calls itself on a smaller version of the same problem until it hits a base case. Trees are just nested recursive structures.
The Template (memorize this shape)
function solve($problem) {
    // 1. BASE CASE — stop recursion
    if (isSmallEnough($problem)) {
        return directAnswer($problem);
    }
    // 2. RECURSIVE CASE — shrink the problem
    $smaller = shrink($problem);
    return combine(solve($smaller));
}
Where This Pattern Lives in Your Work
Use case	Tree structure	Traversal type
Ableton project folder scan	Nested directories / files	DFS — depth-first, pre-order
TFN_MUSIC_COLLECTION.xml import	XML element hierarchy	DFS — recursive element parsing
CMS nested categories	Parent → child taxonomy
DFS or BFS depending on render need
JAOS folder organization	Project > Stems > Samples > Clips	DFS — walk and rename/recolor
File versioning chain	parent_id linked list / tree	Tail recursion or iterative walk

