 Pattern 4 — Graph Traversal (BFS & DFS)
CORE IDEA: A graph is any set of nodes connected by edges. BFS finds the shortest path. DFS explores all possibilities. Most "relation" problems are graphs in disguise.
BFS vs DFS — When to Use Which
	BFS	DFS
Data structure	Queue (FIFO)	Stack or recursion
Finds	Shortest path	All paths / deep exploration
Memory	Wide — keeps level	Deep — keeps one path
Your use case	"What producers are within 2 hops of AJ?"	"What is every possible collaboration path?"
Producer Collaboration Graph Example
// BFS: find all producers reachable within $maxHops from $startId
function bfsProducers(array $graph, int $startId, int $maxHops): array {
    $queue   = [[$startId, 0]];  // [nodeId, depth]
    $visited = [$startId => true];
    $result  = [];
    while (!empty($queue)) {
        [$node, $depth] = array_shift($queue);
        if ($depth > $maxHops) break;
        $result[] = $node;
        foreach ($graph[$node] ?? [] as $neighbor) {
            if (!isset($visited[$neighbor])) {
                $visited[$neighbor] = true;
                $queue[] = [$neighbor, $depth + 1];
            }
        }
    }
    return $result;
}
